> Hi Example,
>  
> John here again from Block Transfer.
>  
> Want to know how Duke Energy lost $1B in shareholder value,
> all because of an erratic accounting mishap?
>  
> Before starting the first SEC-approved blockchain transfer agent,
> I ran a small friends/family hedge fund that returned over 2.4X.
>  
> There, I met Joe Crap
> ster, Head of Shareholder Services at Duke.
>  
> (That's right, Duke is one of the handful of public American
> companies that still act as their own transfer agent.)
>  
> Joe told me that Duke has countless retired shareholders,
> many from the company's own DSPP.
>  
> Subsequently, the board decided not to hire a 'big-name'
> agent that would offer poor investor service.
>  
> Nowadays, that's an unfortunate choice some big
> shareholder-focused firms face given most:
> * ordinary stock transfers execute in days at best,
> * institutional/trust transfers demand limitless paperwork, and
> * manual transfer support is shoddy on a good day...
> (not to mention stiff per-account fees)
>  
> But when covid hit, everything changed...
>  
> APRIL, 2020
>  
> Joe Crapster sweats profusely as hundreds of shareholder emails flood his inbox.
>  
> Phones ring off the hook all day long for his team of nearly a dozen shareholder-service reps.
>  
> The mounting pressure feels like a blood vessel about to explode.
>  
> Joe has no clue how to balance out hundreds of millions of outstanding-yet-unsettled dividend payments. 
>  
> Postal Services effectively came to a standstill once workers stayed home for covid.
>  
> Thus, hundreds of dividend checks mailed to book-entry shareholders are nowhere to be seen, weeks later.
>  
> Securityholders around the world call in livid, all with the same question: "Where's my money?''
>  
> That's a question asked far too often in the transfer agent industry. 
>  
>  
> Even with the best of intentions, most centralized transfer agents are unfortunately vulnerable
> to lapses by the post office, bank branch staff, or internal share accountants.
>  
> What if you could quickly and securely transfer Google stock automatically without medallion certificates?
>  
> If you're open to a quick conversation, book a time below, and
> I'll happily share the rest of Joe's story with you.
> Here's a quick Calendly link. https://calendly.com/block-transfer/wooten-intro
>  
>  
>  
> In good faith,
